Krita Nova 63 - Android: the Brush Panel is exempt from palm rejection

Fingers that land on the Brush Panel are no longer subject to palm
rejection, wherever the pen or a palm is:
- KisMainWindow tells MainActivity where the panel is (setBrushPanelRect,
  in the physical pixels of the Qt view; empty while it is hidden).
- MainActivity reports every finger that lands there to Krita (before, only
  fingers made while the pen was in use), and PanelFingerRouter hands it to
  the widget under it unless Qt delivered it itself.
- A quick tap on the panel (under 0.5 s, hardly moved) that Android's own
  palm rejection cancels still counts as a tap (new action CancelledTap).

